results.gap:
The state offers only reference paper and Excel forms for the records: the facility and animal check record, breeding record, trade record, per-animal ledger and health certificates (Saitama 狭山保健所 guide). Only the yearly report can be e-filed, through LoGo in Tokyo and Saitama. Software could:
- total the report from the ledger and flag unusual death counts (a rise in deaths can lead to an order to submit death certificates);
- warn on the breeding limits (dogs: mating up to age 6 and at most 6 litters; cats: mating up to age 6; the age-7 exception needs proof from the breeding record);
- track deadlines that get no reminders (5-year registration renewal, yearly responsible-person training, yearly report, microchip deadlines);
- prepare microchip entries for the 環境省 portal, which is one animal at a time at ¥400 each, with no bulk upload mentioned;
- keep 5 years of records ready for inspection (19,135 inspections at 15,034 sites in FY2023).
No direct complaints or paid filing-help consultants were found, so the evidence of pain is indirect.

results.price:
All prices are untested estimates:
- dog and cat breeder or small shop: about ¥1,980-2,980 a month (¥24,000-36,000 a year);
- boarding, training or exhibition site: about ¥980 a month for check and trade records;
- chains: about ¥36,000 a year per site;
- report-only season pack: ¥4,980.
No accountant or 行政書士 market was found, so per-accountant pricing does not apply. Benchmarks: registration costs ¥15,000 per category every 5 years, the maximum fine is ¥200,000, and generic POS costs up to ¥15,000 a month.

results.revenue:
About ¥21M a year (about US$140,000) in year 3:
- dog and cat sellers: 16,886 × 3% = 507 × ¥30,000 = ¥15.2M;
- other sellers, exhibitors, renters and 譲受飼養: about 11,600 × 1.5% = 174 × ¥20,000 = ¥3.5M;
- boarding and training only: about 20,000 (unverified) × 1% = 200 × ¥12,000 = ¥2.4M.
At only ¥1,000 a month, the total falls to about ¥10M.
